# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ── Virtual environments ─────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
# the packaging venv (CPU-only torch + a hand-copied CUDA llama_cpp). it is
# built for this machine's GPU/driver combo, so it is never shared.
.venv-build/

# ── Node / Frontend ──────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.eslintcache
*.local
*-debug.log*

# ── Rust / Tauri (desktop shell) ─────────────────────────
# build artifacts; Cargo.lock IS committed (it's an application).
# the configured build also targets an external CARGO_TARGET_DIR.
target/
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/
*.pdb

# ── Portable desktop build (~2.2 GB) ─────────────────────
# the shipped artifact: ThinkStack.exe + the frozen python sidecar, which
# carries this machine's CUDA llama.cpp DLLs and a .env pinned to a local
# model path. rebuild it with scripts, never commit it.
dist-portable/

# ── Local data & runtime state (recreated on startup) ────
# uploaded papers, the vector store, and the persisted model
# selection (data/active_model.txt) all live here
data/

# ── Model weights (kept outside the repo; ignore if copied in) ──
*.gguf

# ── Environment variables ────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Wheels / build artifacts ─────────────────────────────
*.whl

# ── LaTeX build outputs (keep .tex and .pdf) ─────────────
docs/*.aux
docs/*.log
docs/*.out
docs/*.toc
docs/*.synctex.gz

# ── IDE / Editor / OS ────────────────────────────────────
# ignore local .vscode noise but SHARE the workspace config that fixes the
# YAML-extension false positives on the reusable workflows (settings.json pins
# the canonical GitHub Actions schema; extensions.json recommends the linters).
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*.suo
*.sln
*~
.DS_Store

#local
local/
docs/superpowers/specs

# Logs and git helper/scratch files
backend.log
git_branches.txt
git_log_output.txt

# ── Playwright MCP scratch snapshots (browser-tool artifacts) ──
.playwright-mcp/

# ── PyInstaller build artifacts ──────────────────────────
thinkstack-api.spec
*.spec

# ── Tauri sidecar binaries (built, not committed) ────────
src-tauri/bin/

# ── Tauri updater signing keys (NEVER commit the private key) ──
# the private key belongs at ~/.tauri/ and in a CI secret, never in the repo.
# the PUBLIC key is safe and lives in src-tauri/tauri.conf.json.
*.key
!*.key.pub

# on-disk temp for AppImage builds (RAM-backed /tmp is too small)
.build-tmp/

# ── Downloaded dev tools (fetched on demand, not committed) ──
# actionlint: the GitHub Actions linter binary, pulled by CI and for local runs.
/actionlint

# scratch design notes from AI tooling: kept locally, not part of the repo.
# (docs/academic/ IS tracked - it is the project's coursework record.)
docs/superpowers/

# appimage extraction scratch (scripts/build.sh, --appimage-extract)
squashfs-root/

# bundled TeX engine + warm package cache (fetched by scripts/fetch-tex.sh)
data/tex/

# local working notes, never shared
TODO.md

# ── Local-only docs and scratch design artifacts ─────────
# Personal reference material and prototypes that live on this machine. The
# SHARED docs stay tracked: docs/*.md, docs/TEAM/, and docs/academic/ (the
# coursework record) are the project's documentation and are committed.
#
# Anything listed here must NOT appear in src-tauri/tauri.conf.json
# bundle.resources -- the bundler errors on a resource path it cannot find, so
# an ignored file that CI is told to bundle turns into a broken CI build.
docs/LitGraph.pdf
docs/ThinkStack Design Philosophy.pdf
docs/litchart.html
docs/litgraph-demo.html
litgraph-app.png

# Screenshots taken while checking the interface, and the browser automation's
# own output. Both land at the repo root by default. They are evidence for a
# conversation, not part of the product.
#
# Anchored to the root on purpose: src-tauri/icons/ is the app's real artwork
# and stays tracked.
/*.png
.playwright-mcp/
